("event/history-overflow" :names (":HISTORY-OVERFLOW") :kind :event :kind-name "Event" :package "LUT" :summary "Standalone entry or shared TEXT-BUFFER: plist :OPERATION (:EDIT/:UNDO/:REDO), :STACK (:UNDO/:REDO), :CHARACTERS and :LIMIT after a committed range record exceeds a positive character budget and positive record limit. By default the destination stack is empty; HISTORY-RETAIN-NEWEST-P T retains that oversized record alone, with the same feedback. Zero limits and ordinary eviction of older records are silent. Shared buffers notify after :EDIT/:CHANGE under the same reentrancy guard; standalone entries notify before the operation's :CHANGE, when applicable. Errors propagate without rolling back committed content/history." :position 412073)
